    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is async/await?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Async/await enables writing asynchronous code that looks synchronous, improving responsiveness without blocking threads."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "async marks a method as asynchronous. await pauses execution until the task completes, without blocking the thread. Enables responsive applications and efficient resource usage."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Async/Await Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public async Task<User> GetUserAsync(int id) {\n    using var client = new HttpClient();\n    var response = await client.GetAsync($\"/api/users/{id}\");\n    var content = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();\n    return JsonSerializer.Deserialize<User>(content);\n}"
      }
    },
